:p {} "The final was no contest as the favored Americans shattered the world record, running 3:16.6.  Britain was hampered when their lead-off runner, " [:a {:href "/athletes/69345"} "George Nicol"] ", pulled up and limped most of his lap, allowing France to garner the silver medal."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Britain’s third runner was " [:a {:href "/athletes/69496"} "James Soutter"] ".  Shortly after the Olympics, in 1913, he forsook track athletics in favor of the gospel ministry, and was ordained the minister of the Scots Kirk in Nairobi, the first Scottish minister in Kenya.  He returned to Scotland in 1917 and became minister of the parish of Whitekirk and Tynninghame, East Lothian, where he served until he retired in 1949.  In early August 1966, he oddly disappeared one day and was never found, being presumed dead on 8 August 1966."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "United States"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "3:23.3 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "3:16.6 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "label label-default"} [:abbrev {:title "World Record"} "WR"]]] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "10"} [:a {:href "/athletes/79030"} "Mel Sheppard"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/78701"} "Ed Lindberg"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/78784"} "Ted Meredith"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/78935"} "Charles Reidpath"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} "France"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FRA.png"}] "FRA"]] [:td {} "3:22.5 (1 h3)"] [:td {} "3:20.7 (2)